#: ../folio-assistant-core/collab/processes/content/public-comment-release.bpmn:89
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The committee and the editor send the announcement through their channels. Comment is open from here until the agreed close. Skill: public-comment."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/collab/processes/content/public-comment-release.bpmn:61
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The draft has passed publication QA and been circulated (Process_Publication), and the review committee decides it should go out for public comment."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/collab/processes/content/public-comment-release.bpmn:107
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The public comment period is over and its release is archived. Accepted changes continue through their change sets."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/collab/processes/content/public-comment-release.bpmn:65
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The review committee and the editor agree when the public comment release goes out and when comment closes. Skill: public-comment."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/collab/processes/content/public-comment-release.bpmn:30
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The whole public comment cycle around the comments themselves. The committee and editor agree a release date; the draft is frozen as a public comment release with fixed line numbers (a PDF and a permanent PC/<version> site); the editor sets up every channel against that release, with instructions and links, and writes the announcement; the public is told; comments come back and are handled one by one in Process_PublicComment; and the release is archived with the review. Called from Process_Publication. Skills: public-comment, document-publishing."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/collab/processes/content/public-comment-release.bpmn:101
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "When comment closes, the release (PDF, PC/<version> site and the channel exports) is archived with the review record, so every comment's citation can still be followed. Run `bun run cat pc:release close`, which changes only the release's release.json; the frozen copy is never rewritten. Skill: document-publishing."
msgstr ""

